ning imperial summons to office and earning the moniker ‘Master Yu the Summoned.’ Upon the founding of Cao Wei, Yu Cheng served as Magistrate of Xiangcheng, while his sons Yu Yi and Yu Dun consolidated the clan's reputation over two generations through classical mastery. The family flourished most through Yu Dun's line: in the Western Jin, Yu Jun and Yu Chun both served as Commandants and Confucian masters, with Yu Chun renowned for boldly confronting the regent Jia Chong with the query, ‘Where is the Duke of Gaoguixiang?’ In the Eastern Jin, Yu Dun's great-grandson Yu Liang governed as imperial consort-regent alongside Wang Dao, ushering the Yu clan of Yingchuan into its zenith."},"talent":{"military":"1","commerce":"4","politics":"8"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":{"name":"庾乘","height":"平均","shape":"一般"},"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1026","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[22,25,78,60,82,85],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1007202","armor":"WP1015205","helmet":"WP1028705"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10215","name":{"zh":"汉末三杰","en":"Three Heroes of the Late Han"},"year":"185","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1026","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[22,25,78,60,82,85],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1007202","armor":"WP1015205","helmet":"WP1028705"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10615","name":{"zh":"十常侍之乱","en":"Turmoil of the Ten Attendants"},"year":"188","month":"11"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1026","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[22,25,78,60,82,85],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP100